(text "NOTES (bench prototype - verify against your exact boards before wiring)\n1. Power: each controller on its own USB cable for bench tests. GND MUST be common between U1 and U2.\n2. Link: short 3.3 V UART, TX/RX crossed: ESP GPIO4 -> XIAO D7(RX), XIAO D6(TX) -> ESP GPIO5.\n   Long helmet cable: insert 2x 3.3 V RS-485 transceivers here (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n3. OLEDs: set Waveshare board jumpers to 4-wire SPI. SCK/MOSI/DC/RST shared, separate CS.\n   Driver is SSD1309 128x64 on the transparent model - confirm on your units.\n4. GPS: ESP UART1 (GPIO17 TX / GPIO18 RX). Module VCC from 5V (onboard LDO); its UART is 3.3 V logic.\n5. I2C: GPIO8 SDA / GPIO9 SCL. MPU6050 AD0=GND -> 0x68, BMP280 SDO=GND -> 0x76. Breakouts\n   normally include pull-ups; if both do, combined pull-up is fine at 3.3 V. If none, add 4.7k to 3V3.\n6. ESP32-S3 pin numbers assume an Espressif DevKitC-1 style board; avoid GPIO19/20 (USB),\n   GPIO43/44 (UART0 console), and strapping pins 0/3/45/46. Re-map if your variant differs.\n7. Unused XIAO pins (D4, D5, D9, 5V) left free for buttons/expansion. 'Blank display' button suggested on D4." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 228.6 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ce8545ed-3c40-43af-a27a-6f8246872e81"))
